# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S09 — THE BACK DOOR  (the PRE-WALL trust quest — sets up S06's reveal)
# One of the "couple of quests for Marco" that happen BEFORE the wall comes down and
# BEFORE you know he has a daughter (reveal timing locked 7/23, Paolo). Marco asks you
# to help him make his place solid, and is strangely, absolutely immovable that the
# back is his alone — do not go around back, the back he does himself. You do not know
# why yet. Honoring a boundary you do not understand is how you earn the trust that
# eventually brings the wall down; prying fails. When S06 later reveals the daughter,
# THIS is what recontextualizes — he was guarding her the whole time. Cast Marco against
# @ROLE neighbor; never named in a spoken line (W8). CLOUT: a quiet neighborly deed is
# #quiet; drawing a crowd to his door is #notable (and rattles him — eyes on his place
# is the opposite of what he asked).

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q001.W8  REWARD THE LISTENER
#   applied: honoring the boundary is only possible if you actually listened to how he said it; prying is what an inattentive player does.
# @STUDY Q001.W1  TRANSACTION-CARRIES-EMOTION
#   applied: making his place solid is the job; earning the wall coming down is what is really happening.
# @STUDY Q021.W2  "YOU CAN'T SAVE EVERYONE" AS THE THESIS
#   applied: you cannot fix his situation, only be trustworthy inside it.
# @STUDY Q001.P8  W8 (reward the listener
#   applied: the port form of rewarding attention: the solution is gated behind having actually heard how he said the back is his alone.
#
# ---- AND THE VOICE PASS (WORDS lane, 8/27/26). DEMO DAY 2. Same structure,
# ---- same branches, same effects, only the WORDS. Card:
# ---- laws/BOHEMIA_VOICE_CARD_8_26_26.md. This scene contracted ZERO times in
# ---- 24 lines and closed two speeches on a sermon.
# @STUDY Q142.W6  SILENCE EXTRACTS
#   applied: the man tells you more by refusing than by explaining, and the branch that respects the door is the branch that earns the only warm thing he says all night.
# @STUDY Q004.N1  NODE SPIRIT_OFFER
#   applied: the game refuses to sell certainty at any depth -- no option anywhere reveals what is behind the back door, and pushing costs instead of paying.
# @STUDY Q152.W5  THE DESPAIR SCENE CHANGES REGISTER, ONCE
#   applied: he is flat and practical the whole way and breaks exactly twice, both mid-word: once stumbling on a thank you, once shouting.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_back_door   The Back Door
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE neighbor  REQ  is=the_neighbor  household=behind_fence

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The man behind the fence wants his place solid before dark. He's strange about the back of it.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Boarded the front and side. Left the back alone, asked nothing. He won't forget that.
  @DO bond neighbor +20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 21 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Job's done, but I brought half the block to his door doing it. Solid house. Rattled man.
  @DO bond neighbor +4
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 22 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Pushed to see the back room. He shut the whole thing down and finished it himself.
  @DO bond neighbor -10

@OBJ 10  "Help the neighbor make his place solid"   target=neighbor

@TALK ask  speaker=neighbor  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Front and side. Before dark. Boards, nails, whatever you've got in that pack. #tired
  @SAY The back I do myself. Always have. And don't, uh. Don't go round back. I'm not being rude to you. Careful is all.
  @OPT "Front and side. You got it."   [gate: none]  -> work  @DO learn respects_the_boundary
  @OPT "What's in the back?"               [gate: none]  -> back
  @OPT (head around back to look)           [gate: none]  -> pry
  @NOVERB "Ask what he is protecting"
@END

@TALK back  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY Look. It's mine. That's it. You can ask again and I'll say it slower. #dread
  @SAY Front's got a gap by the hinge you could put your arm through. Start there.
  @OPT "Fair. Front and side."             [gate: none]  -> work  @DO learn respects_the_boundary
  @OPT (go look anyway)                     [gate: none]  -> pry
@END

@TALK work  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY (you take the front, he takes the back, and for two hours neither of you says anything at all.)
  @SAY Solid. Feels solid. First time in a while. And you didn't ask twice about the back, that's. Yeah. Thanks.
  @OPT "That's what neighbors are for."    [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 20
  @OPT "Someday you'll tell me."          [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 20
  @OPT "Let's make it a thing. Get some others out."  [gate: none]  -> loud
@END

@TALK pry  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY Hey. HEY. I told you the back was mine, I told you plain. Get away from that door. #dread
  @OPT "Okay. Okay. Backing off."      [gate: none]  -> work
  @OPT "What are you so scared of?"         [gate: none]  -> fold
@END

@TALK fold  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY Scared. Yeah. Okay. Go home. I'll do the front myself. #dread
  @OPT "I'm sorry. That was over the line."      [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 22
@END

@TALK loud  speaker=neighbor
  @SAY No. No, no. I said front and side. Not a block party at my door. #tired
  @SAY Work's good. I'm not saying it isn't. But eyes on my place is the one thing I asked you not to do. Send them home.
  @OPT "Right. Sorry. Just us."             [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 21
@END
